These are the steps to remove the "Store Locator" extension from an existing store front application (currently opened project).

# Step 1. First make sure the current project has all the right file structure:
- It has a `components` directory under the project root
- It has the file `index.jsx` under pages/home directory

# Step 2. Delete folders containing store locator code
- Run `rm -rf components/_fake-store-locator`

# Step 3. Apply the following code changes to pages/home/index.jsx. Skip a step if the code change has already been applied.

- Remove the following lines at the end of the const declaration block:
`const StoreLocator = loadable(() => import('../components/_fake-store-locator'))`

- Remove the following line ONLY WHEN `loadable` is no longer referenced
`import loadable from '@loadable/component'`

- Remove the following line in the JSX element return statement
`<StoreLocator />`